  "_comment": "The whole novel, so the map is complete from the first night. It opens WALLED at chapter 0 (readAlong above) and reveals only as you press \"Finished this chapter\" — a complete dataset behind the wall is exactly what that control is for, and you would have to press \"show all\" to spoil yourself. THE CHAPTER NUMBERS ARE A RECONSTRUCTION: the order of the journey is the reliable part, the chapter each beat falls in is an estimate, and the count of 60 is a guess. Coordinates are fractions of data/maps/four-lands.webp, read off the engraved labels.",
  "_places_note": "safehold and havenstead are the two coordinates NOT read off a label — the endpaper does not draw either. Safehold sits just east of the Hollows and Havenstead west of Culhaven on the Silver River, which is where the later editions put them. Move them if you disagree.",
